      "note": "PRISTINE base (2026-11-16): == fixed build.sh output. firstboot masked + /etc/machine-id set (bootstrap id was uninitialized); deploy-default env baked (SERVITOR_BIND=VM_IP, SERVITOR_ROOT=/var/lib/servitor). Ships NO keys and NO extension by design \u2014 the harness boots a COPY and the first sync provisions it (keys + self-contained extension + config). App code in the image is updated in place by sync when the repo app sha changes. Patched in place 2026-11-16 (qemu-nbd): (1) slot0 (uid/gid 9000, home 0700) added \u2014 the doctor PROBE slot, outside the app pool (slot1-16) so the service's uid-gated kills can never SIGTERM the doctor's probe pi child (intermittent code -15); (2) app tree re-synced from the repo \u2014 the update-pending flag fix: a pre-restart doctor FAIL no longer holds the staged restart (provisioning deadlock: the image ships the non-key env defaults, so the pre-restart app's tick-doctor can never pass until the restart injects the keys) and the fully-consumed flag is CLEARED (sync's APPLIED gate + doctor update.waiting key on the file's existence). | Patched in place 2026-11-16 (2nd pass, qemu-nbd): (3) network gateway 10.42.0.0.1 -> 10.42.0.1 (build.sh derived an invalid 5-octet IP; networkd silently dropped it -> guest booted with NO default route -> live-router prompts returned empty assistant turns, exa searches died); (4) systemd-resolved enabled with public upstream (1.1.1.1/9.9.9.9) + stub resolv.conf \u2014 the image shipped resolved DISABLED with a stale NetworkManager resolv.conf, so the guest could not resolve any public name; (5) app tree re-synced from repo (doctor keys-absent per-needle grep fix). Host-side companion fixes: sync.sh mirrors the laptop's panel-hosts pins into the guest /etc/hosts (hairpin NAT: the router's LAN IP is unroutable from the guest) and self-heals the gateway on deploy; sync's env rewriter normalizes newlines (blank lines doubled each sync -> 184MB env -> E2BIG crash loop); harness.service_uptime() uses the monotonic delta; mock router allocates from ufw-allowed range 48700:48799 (guest->host mock was dropped by ufw).",
